It depends on these packages, which npm installs; they are not part of this
repository:
- pdf.js (pdfjs-dist), Copyright Mozilla Foundation, licensed under the Apache
  License, Version 2.0. It bundles, each under its own licence in the package:
  the standard fonts (Foxit fonts, under PDFium's BSD 3-Clause licence, and
  Liberation Sans, under the GPL v2 with a font exception), Adobe's CMaps
  (BSD 3-Clause), and WebAssembly decoders: OpenJPEG (BSD 2-Clause), a JBIG2
  decoder from PDFium (BSD 3-Clause), qcms (MIT) and QuickJS (MIT), with
  Mozilla's code around them (Apache 2.0, BSD 2-Clause and MIT), and an ICC
  profile (CC0). Their licence files are in node_modules/pdfjs-dist.
- @napi-rs/canvas, licensed under the MIT License, a binding to Skia (BSD
  3-Clause). Its platform package lists the Rust crates it is built from, with
  their licences, in sbom.cdx.json.
